# Architecture audit

## Verdict

The architecture is modular in vocabulary, but only partially modular in execution. The strongest seam is the specialist protocol. Most other stages are concrete calls coordinated through `Conductor`, with shared mutable objects and undocumented semantic coupling.

Two central claims are false today:

- A completed run cannot be replayed through a new specialist without a browser because the specialist inputs are not recorded.
- The emitter does not reliably produce a failing regression spec for a real finding.

No files were modified; the worktree remained clean.

## Critical

### 1. Real findings can become passing or irrelevant Playwright specs

The clearest failure is privilege escalation.

The differ deliberately represents an escalation using the blocked policy witness followed by the witness that bypassed it:

> `testimonies=[policy_witness, t]`

[differ.py:91](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/differ.py:91)

The emitter then chooses any non-owner testimony and sorts by context name:

> `return sorted(candidates ... key=lambda t: t.context.name)[0]`

[emitter.py:23](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:23)

For the valid case `anon=blocked, member=reached`, that chooses anonymous and emits:

```ts
storageState: ".auth/anon.json"
expect(blocked).toBeTruthy()
```

That spec passes because anonymous is already blocked; it never tests the member bypass. I confirmed this through a local read-only reproduction.

Other emitter failures:

- `PROPAGATION_FAILURE` and `DEAD_SURFACE` fall through to `test.skip`, so they do not become failing specs at all. [emitter.py:135](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:135)
- Vision-generated render findings do not attach a `Defect`. [layout_i18n.py:211](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/specialists/layout_i18n.py:211) The emitter therefore generates an unconditional `throw`, not a reproducible invariant. [emitter.py:58](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:58)
- The probe records defect detail and selector, but `Witness._map_defects()` discards both and retains only the enum. [probe.js:26](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/probe.js:26), [witness.py:219](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:219)
- Consequently, route findings test `body`, not the offending element. [emitter.py:36](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:36)
- A clipping finding is emitted as an offscreen-viewport assertion, although the probe defines clipping as `scrollWidth > clientWidth` inside an element. [probe.js:95](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/probe.js:95), [emitter.py:66](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:66)
- An RTL geometry failure is reduced to checking `dir="rtl"` and computed direction. A layout can remain completely unmirrored and pass. [emitter.py:98](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:98)

The `Finding` DTO is a real data boundary, but the emitter depends on hidden conventions about testimony ordering, defect provenance, and finding kinds. Replacing the differ while merely returning valid `Finding` objects can silently break emission.

### 2. One compositor leaks visual state across surfaces

The compositor is created once, outside the surface loop:

[conductor.py:84](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:84)

It retains `_latest`, `_thumbnails`, and `_changed_at` for its lifetime:

[compositor.py:53](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/compositor.py:53)

At the next surface, the conductor changes the global action before any new frames arrive:

[conductor.py:93](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:93)

The compositor considers the wall fully painted if every context has ever produced a frame:

```python
return all(name in self._latest for name in self._contexts)
```

[compositor.py:134](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/compositor.py:134)

Therefore, after surface one:

- A silent witness on surface two is represented by its surface-one image.
- A moment can combine new tiles from surface two with stale tiles from surface one.
- That mixed wall is relabelled with surface two using `replace(settled, surface=surface)`. [conductor.py:221](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:221)
- Motion can be attributed to the new action even if the underlying change belongs to the prior generation.

The missing concept is a surface/run epoch. Either reset the compositor per surface or require every tile to paint in the current epoch before emitting.

## High

### 3. The replay claim is false

`Specialist.judge()` requires both moments and testimonies:

[contracts.py:98](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/contracts.py:98)

A completed run persists:

- Mosaic JPEGs.
- A feed containing mosaic sequence, image path, and tile boxes.
- Flattened findings.
- Generated specs.

The mosaic feed payload omits:

- `Moment.changed`
- `Moment.action`
- `Moment.surface`
- `Moment.settled_ms`
- `MosaicFrame.composed_at`

[contracts.py:153](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/contracts.py:153)

No testimony is serialized. `ConductSummary` returns testimonies in memory, but not moments:

[conductor.py:41](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:41)

Once `conduct()` returns, the visual specialist inputs are gone. Once the process exits, testimony inputs are gone too.

A real replay requires a versioned durable record containing:

- Contexts and their varied axes.
- Surface catalogue.
- Every testimony field: outcome, status, paths, signatures, geometry, defects with selector/detail, and observation time.
- Every moment field, referencing its persisted JPEG.
- A loader that reconstructs the exact `Moment` and `Testimony` sequences.
- A browser-free specialist runner.

That codec, manifest, and replay entry point do not exist.

The stronger “sessions do not know who is watching” claim is also overstated. Every witness injects `probe.js`, and the probe itself decides overflow, clipping, contrast, tap-target, and translation defects. [witness.py:78](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:78), [probe.js:55](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/probe.js:55) Adding a lens that needs an unrecorded DOM measurement requires another browser run, not merely a replay.

### 4. Testimony is mutated after observation

`Testimony` claims:

> “Evidence, immutable once written.”

But it is a non-frozen dataclass with mutable lists:

[types.py:182](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/types.py:182)

The conductor runs the mirror judgment and appends its result directly into `variant.defects`:

[conductor.py:102](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:102)

This is unsound for three reasons:

1. A derived comparison result is rewritten as witness-observed evidence.
2. The witness assigned `PARTIAL` when defects existed during observation, but a later mirror defect is appended while the testimony remains `REACHED`. [witness.py:91](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:91)
3. Differ, specialists, emitter, summary, and feed all share references to the same mutable testimony.

The mirror stage should return findings or immutable derived observations. It should not rewrite testimony.

The same independence problem applies to specialists: they run sequentially over the same mutable objects, and the conductor neither copies inputs nor catches specialist exceptions. [conductor.py:108](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:108) One specialist can mutate what the next sees or abort the entire run.

### 5. `AccessSpecialist` duplicates the differ

The conductor always calls `compare(testimonies)`, then calls every specialist:

[conductor.py:108](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:108)

`AccessSpecialist` calls the same `compare()` again and filters it:

[access.py:17](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/specialists/access.py:17)

It adds no independent lens. In the default CLI, it is always installed. [__main__.py:54](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/__main__.py:54)

Effects:

- Privilege findings occur twice in `summary.findings` and the feed.
- Service counts are inflated.
- The console hides the duplication because it deduplicates findings by ID. [app.js:35](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/console/app.js:35)
- `emit_all` writes the same deterministic filename twice and returns duplicate paths. [emitter.py:172](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/emitter.py:172)

This is the pass-through that earns nothing.

## Seams

| Boundary | Assessment | Replacement impact |
|---|---|---|
| Witness → compositor | Real value type, incidental operational seam | `Frame` exists, but witnesses emit `(bytes, metadata)`, not `Frame`; the conductor invents sequence numbers and adapts the callback. Replacing either side requires reproducing undocumented constructor/lifecycle methods and conductor glue. [witness.py:112](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:112), [conductor.py:186](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:186) |
| Compositor → specialist | Mostly genuine | `Moment`/`MosaicFrame` plus the `Specialist` protocol form a useful interface. A specialist can be replaced independently if it remains synchronous and does not throw. The compositor itself is concrete and must still expose the exact constructor, `submit`, `set_action`, and `tick` API. |
| Differ → emitter | Nominal interface, brittle semantics | `Finding` is explicit, but emitter behavior depends on testimony ordering, mutable defects, selectors that were discarded, and a closed set of kinds. Shape-compatible replacement is not behavior-compatible. |
| Conductor → everything | Incidental calls | It directly imports and constructs `Witness` and `Compositor`, invokes concrete functions for mirror/differ/emitter, performs persistence, and mutates evidence. Only specialists have an explicit protocol. [conductor.py:14](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:14) |

The module doing more than its name says is `probe.js`: it is not merely a probe; it is a substantial deterministic specialist running inside every browser witness. The conductor is also more than an ordering owner—it performs discovery, adaptation, mutation, error policy, artifact storage, feed serialization, and emission.

## Concurrency and performance

What protects current shared state:

- Browser isolation comes from separate Playwright contexts.
- Compositor mutations happen on one asyncio event-loop thread.
- `consume()` contains no `await`, so sequence increment and `submit()` are currently atomic relative to other asyncio tasks. [conductor.py:192](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/conductor.py:192)
- There is no compositor lock; use from threads or a consumer that introduces awaits would invalidate that assumption.

Remaining races and losses:

- Every CDP frame creates an unbounded task. There is no queue bound, coalescing, or backpressure. [witness.py:121](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:121)
- `stop_screencast()` cancels all pending delivery tasks, so terminal frames can disappear when navigation finishes. [witness.py:141](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:141)
- Sequence numbers describe consumer execution order, not capture time; `Frame.captured_at` and CDP metadata are ignored.
- The cross-surface stale-wall race described above is not protected.
- A live feed reader can observe a partial JSON line. The console records that partial file text, then slices it away on the next poll, potentially losing the completed event permanently. [app.js:95](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/console/app.js:95)

The whole-wall encode was moved off every `submit`, which is a good correction. The hot path is still synchronous:

- Base64 decode in the asyncio task. [witness.py:184](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/witness.py:184)
- JPEG decode, RGB conversion, LANCZOS resize/crop, grayscale resize, and pixel diff on every frame. [compositor.py:88](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/compositor.py:88)
- Full 4×2 wall construction and JPEG encoding inside `tick()` on the event loop. [compositor.py:138](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/compositor.py:138)
- The browser probe forces repeated DOM/style/layout reads across large element sets in seven renderer contexts. [probe.js:55](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/probe.js:55)

A slow consumer cannot block the CDP callback itself, but its synchronous PIL work still blocks the shared Python event loop and lets delivery tasks accumulate.

## Three weakest tests

1. `test_public_spec_example_is_emitted_from_a_real_finding`

   [test_demo_suite.py:92](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/tests/test_demo_suite.py:92)

   The “real finding” is manually constructed with owner and anonymous both reached. Under the differ’s policy rules, that evidence does not produce an escalation because no blocked witness establishes a policy. [run_demo_suite.py:128](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/scripts/run_demo_suite.py:128) The test would pass if the differ stopped producing escalations or if the generated spec passed immediately.

2. `test_each_finding_kind_emits_the_required_assertion`

   [test_emitter.py:72](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/tests/test_emitter.py:72)

   It checks substrings such as `toBeTruthy()` and `status() === 403`. It does not execute or type-check the specs, nor verify which witness is selected. It passes despite the confirmed blocked-anonymous/wrong-context escalation bug and treats a skipped dead-surface test as successful emission.

3. `test_final_flush_never_publishes_a_wall_with_an_unpainted_context`

   [test_conductor.py:305](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/tests/test_conductor.py:305)

   It tests only the first surface. On a later surface, a silent witness is considered painted because its previous-surface frame remains in `_latest`; the named “never” invariant is therefore broken while this test still passes.

A broader gap is that the browser “end-to-end” tests prove the demo defects exist, but do not run those sites through Conductor and execute the emitted Playwright specs. [test_plants_end_to_end.py:1](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/tests/test_plants_end_to_end.py:1)

## What I would delete

Outright:

- `AccessSpecialist` and its default registrations. The differ already owns this judgment, and the wrapper actively creates duplicate findings.
- The `Compositor.mosaic` alias; it is an unused pass-through over `current_mosaic`. [compositor.py:72](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/compositor.py:72)
- The invalid hand-built “real finding” example; regenerate examples only from actual differ output.

I would also remove `RealtimeSpecialist` from the default specialist list immediately. Ordinary conductor testimonies are deliberately filtered out, so it is a default no-op. [realtime.py:28](/home/dev/parallax-lanes/audit-arch/src/parallax/specialists/realtime.py:28) `RelationalPair` independently produces propagation findings and is not wired into the conductor. Until there is a declared sender/action/receiver/expectation event contract, inferring causality from later tile motion is not defensible.
